WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.000
This is a re-run I screen-recorded after the fact. The original baseline runs were earlier on 2 Oct.

00:05.000 --> 00:07.000
Output side: my Google Cloud Storage bucket, where Rhombus writes the cleaned file.

00:07.000 --> 00:09.000
Input side: my S3 bucket. The pipeline always reads input/orders.csv.

00:09.000 --> 00:13.000
Step 1: upload the normal (baseline) file as orders.csv.

00:13.000 --> 00:15.000
Same file name every time, so the pipeline never changes. Only the data does.

00:15.000 --> 00:18.000
Upload done. S3 keeps every version, so I can prove which file each run used.

00:18.000 --> 00:26.000
Step 2: run the pipeline in Rhombus. I run it by hand because scheduled runs never fired on my account (reported to Rhombus).

00:26.000 --> 00:28.000
"Pipeline completed successfully."

00:28.000 --> 00:33.000
Step 3: the cleaned file lands in Google Cloud Storage as a new, timestamped CSV.

00:33.000 --> 00:38.000
Next I download it and check it with my own validator. The baseline gave byte-identical output 3 runs in a row.
